    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.deps\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently the `MiniDeps.add` function will download the plugin if it is not present on the disk, and add the plugin to the runtime path. There is no separate commands to download plugins based on its source information regardless of whether or not this plugin should be loaded.\r\n\r\nI would like to add an command for downloading plugins. This is useful why I lazy load plugins based on, for example, filetypes. Currently, if I add a filetype autocmd to lazy load a plugin, this plugin will be downloaded first, and then added to rtp. This could be a bit cumbersome if I would like the plugin to be loaded instantly so that I can start working on my file immediately.\r\n\r\nIf we have a command for downloading plugins based on their source info, I can first download all plugins, and then when they need to be loaded, they will be loaded instantly without users realizing that it is being downloaded/loaded.",
    "closed_at": "2024-10-28T14:36:08Z",
