        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n> If we have a command for downloading plugins based on their source info, I can first download all plugins, and then when they need to be loaded, they will be loaded instantly without users realizing that it is being downloaded/loaded.\r\n\r\nI don't think I fully understand the use case you describe. Using the current `add()` will download plugin only one time (per machine configuration) and will add it to runtimepath without downloading afterwards. Do you say that you'd like to have a functionality to even avoid it downloading the first time in exchange of downloading it once during some initial config setup?",
