        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the follow up!\r\n\r\nI think I am going to close this in favor of suggesting to use `add()` in the same way as you'd expect to use its \"only download\" part. Here is some reasoning:\r\n- Downloading happens only once and I don't think this is a huge inconvenience for users. Moreover, I'd say that the current behavior is beneficial in a sense that the plugin *fully* lazy loaded: it is not even downloaded if it is not used.\r\n- Implementing \"download all at once but load only on filetype/keystroke/etc.\" needs either a separate custom run with downloading all plugins (in which case using `:DepsAdd` should be enough, with possible Neovim restart afterwards) or duplicated separate code lines for downloading and adding (which I'd personally not encourage).\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
            "created_at": "2024-10-28T14:36:08Z",
